Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::cq_pop_stays_in_bounds_and_flips_only_at_the_wrap`.

The defect: `CompletionQueue::pop` wraps the head but forgets to flip the expected phase, so every lap after
the first reads stale entries as fresh.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(queue.phase != phase, queue.head == 0)`.

